                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "mortaises"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "cb90a4b4-3644-4e65-8af1-094ae265595d",
                        "entry_id": "d5242a90-eee1-3d2f-abd0-8a1ad432b4fc",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "mortoise"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3d08508a-42ce-3773-996b-4bfa13ca0fe7",
                        "entry_id": "d5242a90-eee1-3d2f-abd0-8a1ad432b4fc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Entaille, généralement de section rectangulaire, pratiquée dans une pièce de bois ou de métal pour y recevoir le tenon d’une autre pièce quand on veut les assembler."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "08165863-7a2b-4629-a1c9-8cab063763ce",
                                "sense_id": "3d08508a-42ce-3773-996b-4bfa13ca0fe7",
                                "text": "Les deux longs côtés de la mortaise qui répondent à la largeur du tenon , doivent toujours être dirigés parallèlement au fil du bois."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cfd4974d-ae80-4e5d-bd57-3732b4e63f3b",
                                "sense_id": "3d08508a-42ce-3773-996b-4bfa13ca0fe7",
                                "text": "Quand on veut que la cheville fasse tirage, on perce d’abord la mortaise de part en part, le tenon n’y étant pas ; on met le tenon en place, on marque les trous, on retire le tenon, on perce les trous un peu plus haut qu’ils ne doivent l’être."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f6bb2271-cbac-4a12-98b0-82400f953f47",
                                "sense_id": "3d08508a-42ce-3773-996b-4bfa13ca0fe7",
                                "text": "Lorsque le tenon joue dans la mortaise, l'assemblage se trouve promptement détruit par les efforts auxquels il est nécessairement soumis."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7d94f530-8d0c-35db-acd9-b83ff6e61ae2",
                        "entry_id": "d5242a90-eee1-3d2f-abd0-8a1ad432b4fc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Vide d'un moufle où l'on met le rouet, trou dans lequel passe la tête du mât de hune."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "090e6ec9-f874-40f8-8ab2-29b5614b126d",
                        "source_entry_id": "d5242a90-eee1-3d2f-abd0-8a1ad432b4fc",
                        "target_lang_word": "mortise",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mortise",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e0491f6-fb99-3e66-9c3a-b74fb49bcd6e",
                                        "entry_id": "591d9188-6cb1-3e6f-8fa4-0f71cb1a7e1b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A hole that is made to receive a tenon so as to form a joint."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f1a950e-11ef-4ae2-99ab-eba545abcd47",
                                                "sense_id": "9e0491f6-fb99-3e66-9c3a-b74fb49bcd6e",
                                                "text": "If there is much gauging for the same size mortise and tenon to be done, and if a mortise gauge is not handy, a simple improvised gauge for the purpose can easily be made with two pieces of wood and four or five steel sprigs…"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff1342fe-4b60-4bc1-8ffc-aad2d86ec673",
                                                "sense_id": "9e0491f6-fb99-3e66-9c3a-b74fb49bcd6e",
                                                "text": "A keyed mortise-and-tenon joint is constructed the same as a doweled mortise and tenon joint except that the tenon projects far enough through the mortise to admit the insertion of a tapering key which draws the mortised piece firmly against the shoulder of the tenon."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1df91558-43a1-357f-a46d-3301c10d8a21",
                                        "entry_id": "591d9188-6cb1-3e6f-8fa4-0f71cb1a7e1b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Stability; power of adhesion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "mortise",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "02b099bf-71e8-3778-affb-8af38fce33f2",
                                        "entry_id": "f0e4107a-7fb2-3b0c-9e49-06de65233434",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cut a mortise in."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d91c511-fb3b-44ea-bfbd-1765cd81d60c",
                                                "sense_id": "02b099bf-71e8-3778-affb-8af38fce33f2",
                                                "text": "A keyed mortise-and-tenon joint is constructed the same as a doweled mortise and tenon joint except that the tenon projects far enough through the mortise to admit the insertion of a tapering key which draws the mortised piece firmly against the shoulder of the tenon."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f803ae48-db78-3b4b-b695-7c24a1c0c1e7",
                                        "entry_id": "f0e4107a-7fb2-3b0c-9e49-06de65233434",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To join by a mortise and tenon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73966734-58bc-4ca7-9812-7112a552bf6f",
                                                "sense_id": "f803ae48-db78-3b4b-b695-7c24a1c0c1e7",
                                                "text": "Sculptures from Mohenjodaro and Tell Asmar in 2400 B.C. show wheels consisting of three pieces of wood mortised together, and bound with leather tyres which were attached with copper nails. These wheels turned in one piece with the axle, which was secured to the body of the sledge with leather thongs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4efca79d-b118-3496-8e3a-ae481ed0d9f3",
                                        "entry_id": "f0e4107a-7fb2-3b0c-9e49-06de65233434",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To adjust the horizontal space between selected pairs of letters; to kern."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
